$$\mathbb E\sum_{i=1}^KS^i=\sum_{i=1}^n\mathbb E[S^i]\mathbb P(K\ge i).$$
Since $\mathbb E[S^i]=(n+i-1)!/(n-1)!$, the $i$th term is $\binom{n+i-1}{i}$, proving the formula.

