$$r=\frac{r_0}{1+e\cos\theta},\qquad r_0=\frac{l^2}{k}.$$
Consequently
$$l=\sqrt{kr_0},\qquad E=\frac{mk(e^2-1)}{2r_0}.$$

See also: <Kepler orbit>, <Binet equation>, <Orbital eccentricity>.

