$$\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\frac{\cos(nx)}{x^4+1}\,dx
=\frac\pi{\sqrt2}e^{-n/\sqrt2}\left(\cos\frac n{\sqrt2}+\sin\frac n{\sqrt2}\right).$$

See also: <Residue theorem>, <Jordan lemma>.

