= Solution
{parent=d}

Let $g_i=E_i[T_A\mathbf1_{\{T_A<T_F\}}]$ for the chain absorbed at $A$ or $F$. With $g_C=g_D=y$, first-step analysis gives
$$g_B=(2+2y)/3,qquad g_E=(1+2y)/3,qquad y=(1+g_B+g_E)/2.$$
Thus $y=3$ and $g_B=8/3$. Including the initial step from $A$, the conditional mean is
$$1+\frac{g_B}{h_B}=1+\frac{8/3}{2/3}=5.$$

See also: <Conditional hitting time>, <First-step analysis>.

