The pointwise limit is $f(x)=e^x/\cosh(ax)$ and
$$|f_n-f|=(e^{1/n}-1)\frac{e^x}{\cosh(ax)}.$$
The final factor is bounded on $\mathbb R$ exactly when $|a|\ge1$; when $|a|<1$ it diverges as $x\to+\infty$. Thus convergence is uniform exactly for $|a|\ge1$.

See also: <Uniform convergence>, <Asymptotic comparison of exponential functions>.

