The likelihood is $\theta e^{-\theta X}$. Multiplication by the prior gives a density proportional to $\theta^m e^{-(\lambda+X)\theta}$, so
$$\theta\mid X\sim\Gamma(m+1,\lambda+X)$$
in shape-rate parametrisation.

See also: <Gamma-exponential conjugacy>, <Bayesian posterior>.

