= Solution
{parent=b}

Squared-error posterior risk is minimized by the posterior mean. Hence
$$\hat\theta_{\rm Bayes}=E[\theta\mid X]=\frac{m+1}{\lambda+X}.$$

See also: <Bayes estimator under squared error loss>.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= c
{parent=6h}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=c}

Put $k=m+1$ and $L=\lambda+X$. The posterior risk is
$$\tfrac12\{e^{-ra}M(r)+e^{ra}M(-r)\},$$
where $M(s)=(L/(L-s))^k$. Differentiating in $a$ gives
$$e^{2ra}=\frac{M(r)}{M(-r)}=\left(\frac{L+r}{L-r}\right)^k.$$
Thus
$$\hat\theta=\frac{m+1}{2r}\log\frac{\lambda+X+r}{\lambda+X-r}.$$

See also: <Bayes estimator>, <Posterior expected loss>.

