A set is convex when it contains every segment joining two of its points. A function on a convex set is convex when
$$f(tx+(1-t)y)\le tf(x)+(1-t)f(y)$$
for all $x,y$ and $0\le t\le1$.

See also: <Convex set>, <Convex function>.

