= Solution
{parent=a}

The minimal polynomial $m_\phi$ is the unique monic polynomial of least positive degree with $m_\phi(\phi)=0$. Uniqueness follows because division of one monic annihilator by another would produce a lower-degree annihilator. Cayley–Hamilton says that the characteristic polynomial annihilates $\phi$; division then shows
$$m_\phi\mid\chi_\phi.$$

See also: <Minimal polynomial>, <Cayley-Hamilton theorem>.

