= Solution
{parent=b}

The map $\theta:\mathbb C[x]\to V$, $p\mapsto p(\phi)a_1$, is surjective because $1,x,\ldots,x^{n-1}$ map to the given basis. Its kernel is generated by the minimal polynomial and the quotient has dimension $n$, so $\deg m_\phi=n$. The relation for $\phi(a_n)$ gives
$$m_\phi(x)=x^n-\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}c_{k+1}x^k.$$

See also: <Cyclic vector>, <Companion matrix>, <Minimal polynomial>.

