{parent=b}

For every probability vector $x$, antisymmetry gives $x^TAx=0$. Applying the minimax inequalities with the same strategy on both sides shows the lower value is at most zero and the upper value at least zero; transposition also changes the value to its negative. Hence the value is zero.

See also: <Antisymmetric zero-sum game>.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= c
{parent=19h}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=c}

Starting from any optimal strategy, transfer all probability on row $i_0$ to row $i_1$. Every payoff against a pure column weakly increases, so the security level remains optimal. The resulting strategy has $p_{i_0}=0$.

See also: <Dominated strategy>.

