Uniformly for the arguments involved,
$$\log\frac{\sin x}{x}=-\frac{x^2}{6}+O(x^4).$$
Hence
$$\log\phi_{n^{-3/2}S_n}(\xi)
=-\frac{\xi^2}{6n^3}\sum_{j=1}^nj^2
+O\left(\frac{\xi^4}{n^6}\sum_{j=1}^nj^4\right)
\longrightarrow-\frac{\xi^2}{18},$$
because $n^{-3}\sum j^2\to1/3$ and the error is $O(n^{-1})$. The limiting characteristic function is that of $N(0,1/9)$. Lévy's theorem gives
$$n^{-3/2}S_n\Rightarrow N(0,1/9).$$

See also: <Small-argument sine product asymptotic>, <Characteristic-function convergence theorem>.

